The proposed answer is incorrect. In July 1898, Marie and Pierre Curie announced the discovery of **polonium**, named after Marie's native Poland. Their paper "Sur une substance nouvelle radio-active, contenue dans la pechblende" was presented to the Académie des Sciences on July 18, 1898.

Radium was discovered later that same year — the Curies, working with Gustave Bémont, announced it in December 1898. The proposed answer gets the sequence backwards, though it correctly notes Bémont's collaboration, which applies to the radium work, not polonium.

